course: dictionary
lesson: 11788
title: Words for people, places and languages
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where a person, a thing or a language comes from. Belarusian is one of them. It can describe something: «We ate Belarusian pancakes at the market.» Here it tells you which kind of pancakes they were.
explain: It can also name a person: «Olga is a Belarusian, and she lives in Minsk.» A Belarusian is someone from Belarus, a country in eastern Europe. More than one person is Belarusians. Always write Belarusian with a capital B, like English or French.
explain: The same word can name a language: «Olga speaks Belarusian at home.» Belarusian is a Slavic language, close to Ukrainian and Russian. When you read the news, Belarus may be mentioned as an ally of Russia, and the words Belarusian and Belarusians tell you about its people.
fact: Belarus is a country in eastern Europe. Its capital is Minsk.
fact: Belarus lies between Poland, Lithuania, Latvia, Russia and Ukraine.
fact: «Belarusian» can be an adjective, a noun for a person, or the name of a language.
fact: A person from Belarus is «a Belarusian». More than one is «Belarusians».
fact: Belarusian, the language, is a Slavic language close to Ukrainian and Russian.
exercise: «The Belarusian team won the match.» In this sentence, Belarusian tells us where the team comes from. What kind of word is it here? | Noun for a language | Verb | Noun for a person | *Adjective, describing the team
exercise: Minsk is the capital of which country? | Lithuania | Poland | Latvia | *Belarus
exercise: «Anya is a Belarusian.» What is a Belarusian? | *A person from Belarus | A kind of bread | A language spoken only in Poland | A river in Russia
test: Which word is the plural, meaning more than one person from Belarus? | Belaruses | *Belarusians | Belarus | Belarusian
test: Which word completes the sentence? «Olga speaks ___ at home.» | Belarus | Minsk | *Belarusian | Belarusians
exam: Which sentence uses Belarusian correctly? | We visited a Belarus village. | We visited a Belarusians village. | *We visited a Belarusian village. | We visited a belarusian village.
